From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a Linux window opened over another keeps the keys on a busy machine

A Linux Terminal opened while Notepad was the active window was active, but
the keys typed went to Notepad -- now and then, more often the busier the
machine (linuxembed-gate failed so on the release and on the development
build under load). Taking the program's window into its frame reparents
it, and the X server unmaps and maps it again as it goes; the frame heard
both (it listens to the window's structure first) and explorer hid the
frame and showed it again (0788 made it active again after). Hidden for a
moment, the window behind it -- Notepad -- was made the active window, and
its program, told late on a busy machine, gave its window the X focus
after the terminal had it.

The frame now listens to the program's window from when it is in the frame
and shown, not to its own reparenting: the frame stays shown and active,
and nothing else is made active meanwhile.

Test: test/linuxembed-gate.sh 11 (a foreground log of the windows made
active as the new window is framed: Notepad must not be among them after
it; the X focus and typed keys too). Mutant SG_MUTANT_EMBED_REPARENT_HIDES
fails it. The gate is also made sturdier: xterm no longer waits on the
real session's session manager (SESSION_MANAGER unset), the list names no
killed window whose X id the next xterm may get, the new window is waited
for until framed, the shell's start by its desktop window, and the probe's
Z-order walk is bounded.
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
@@ -470,10 +470,22 @@
      * not with our frame */
     X11DRV_expect_error( data->display, ignore_error, NULL );
     XAddToSaveSet( data->display, child );
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_EMBED_REPARENT_HIDES
     XSelectInput( data->display, child, StructureNotifyMask | PropertyChangeMask );
+#endif
     XReparentWindow( data->display, child, data->whole_window, x, y );
     XResizeWindow( data->display, child, w, h );
     XMapRaised( data->display, child );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_EMBED_REPARENT_HIDES
+    /* What the program's window does from now on is heard -- not the unmap
+     * and map of its being reparented here: heard, the frame was hidden and
+     * shown again (explorer's WM_SG_EMBED_SHOWN), the window behind it made
+     * active meanwhile and the frame again after (0788) -- but that window's
+     * program, told late (a busy machine), took the X focus after the
+     * frame's program had it: typing in a Linux Terminal just opened over
+     * Notepad went to Notepad (linuxembed-gate, 2026-10-05). */
+    XSelectInput( data->display, child, StructureNotifyMask | PropertyChangeMask );
+#endif
 #ifndef SG_MUTANT_EMBED_WITHDRAWN
     {
         /* shown, as a window manager says of the windows it frames: the
